---
import ProductLayout from '../layouts/ProductLayout.astro';

const description = 'Automated recovery drills and verification for Kubernetes applications and PostgreSQL. Design drills, measure RTO/RPO, and prove data correctness from V0 to V4.';
---
<ProductLayout title="Recovery, verified" description={description} current="overview">
  <section class="hero-band">
    <div class="hero-grid" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="page-wrap hero-wrap">
      <div class="hero-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-accent"><span class="pulse-dot"></span> PRE-ALPHA</span>
        <span class="badge">V0–V4 VERIFICATION</span>
        <span class="badge">KUBERNETES & POSTGRESQL</span>
        <a class="badge badge-link" href="https://github.com/jagarkarlo/checkride" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor"><path fill-rule="evenodd" clip-rule="evenodd" d="M12 2C6.477 2 2 6.484 2 12.017c0 4.425 2.865 8.18 6.839 9.504.5.092.682-.217.682-.483 0-.237-.008-.868-.013-1.703-2.782.605-3.369-1.343-3.369-1.343-.454-1.158-1.11-1.466-1.11-1.466-.908-.62.069-.608.069-.608 1.003.07 1.53 1.032 1.53 1.032.892 1.53 2.341 1.088 2.91.832.092-.647.35-1.088.636-1.338-2.22-.253-4.555-1.113-4.555-4.951 0-1.093.39-1.988 1.029-2.688-.103-.253-.446-1.272.098-2.65 0 0 .84-.27 2.75 1.026A9.564 9.564 0 0112 6.844c.85.004 1.705.115 2.504.337 1.909-1.296 2.747-1.027 2.747-1.027.546 1.379.202 2.398.1 2.651.64.7 1.028 1.595 1.028 2.688 0 3.848-2.339 4.695-4.566 4.943.359.309.678.92.678 1.855 0 1.338-.012 2.419-.012 2.747 0 .268.18.58.688.482A10.019 10.019 0 0022 12.017C22 6.484 17.522 2 12 2z"/></svg>
          GITHUB ↗
        </a>
      </div>
      <h1>Backups are a promise.<br /><span>Recovery is the proof.</span></h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">Backup tools report <code>Completed</code>. That proves a backup was written, not that your application will work when restored. Checkride restores workloads into an isolated separate cluster, measures real RTO, and mathematically proves acknowledged data survived (V0–V4).</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="action-primary" href="/demo/index.html#/report">Open the live demo <span>↗</span></a>
        <a class="action-secondary" href="#quickstart">Quick start guide <span>↓</span></a>
        <a class="action-secondary" href="/docs/">Read documentation <span>→</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-status">
        <span class="status-ring">01</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Now: disposable k3d PostgreSQL restore & V0–V4 evidence evaluation</strong>
          <span>Next: unattended orchestration and multi-scenario harness</span>
        </div>
        <span class="status-line"></span>
        <a class="status-end" href="/roadmap/">VIEW ROADMAP ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="signal-band">
    <div class="page-wrap signal-grid">
      <span>NOT A BACKUP PRODUCT</span>
      <span>SEPARATE CLUSTER ISOLATION</span>
      <span>EXACT WRITE LEDGER RPO</span>
      <span>ED25519 ATTESTATION</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="feature-band">
    <div class="page-wrap feature-grid">
      <div class="feature-copy">
        <p class="section-index">01 / THE QUESTION</p>
        <h2>A green job is not a recovered application.</h2>
        <p>A backup can complete while an application loses acknowledged writes, restores the wrong point in time, or fails because CRDs and operators were missing in the recovery cluster. Checkride makes recovery depth explicit, measurable, and reviewable.</p>
        <a class="under-link" href="/evidence/">See what counts as proof <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="signal-graphic" aria-label="Five verification levels from backup status to correct application data">
        <div class="signal-legend"><span>RECOVERY SIGNAL</span><span>V0 — V4</span></div>
        {[
          { id: "V0", label: "Backup status", proof: "Tool reported success", width: 38 },
          { id: "V1", label: "Restore status", proof: "Job finished in cluster", width: 53 },
          { id: "V2", label: "Workload health", proof: "Pods ready, HTTP/TCP 200", width: 66 },
          { id: "V3", label: "Data structure", proof: "Tables, row counts, checksums", width: 82 },
          { id: "V4", label: "Data correctness", proof: "Ledger RPO & business invariants", width: 100 },
        ].map((level, i) => (
          <div class:list={["signal-row", { active: i === 4 }]}>
            <b>{level.id}</b>
            <span>{level.label} <small class="signal-proof">· {level.proof}</small></span>
            <i style={`--signal-width:${level.width}%`}></i>
            <small>{i === 4 ? "DEEP" : "LEVEL"}</small>
          </div>
        ))}
        <p class="signal-foot">A drill reports the deepest contiguous level passed. A failure at V2 stops the chain at V1.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pipeline-band">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-index">02 / HOW IT WORKS</p>
          <h2>Continuous recovery verification, step by step.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="heading-sub">From drill specification to cryptographically attested report.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-steps">
        <div class="pipeline-card">
          <span class="step-num">01</span>
          <h3>Declare drill</h3>
          <p>Versioned YAML spec defines scenario, separate-cluster target, and strict RTO/RPO SLA objectives.</p>
          <code>Drill spec</code>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="pipeline-card">
          <span class="step-num">02</span>
          <h3>Track writes</h3>
          <p>Client acknowledged writes are recorded in an external ledger before disaster injection.</p>
          <code>Write ledger</code>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="pipeline-card">
          <span class="step-num">03</span>
          <h3>Isolated restore</h3>
          <p>Application is recovered into a clean separate cluster, exposing missing CRDs or operators.</p>
          <code>Isolated cluster</code>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="pipeline-card">
          <span class="step-num">04</span>
          <h3>Verify V0–V4</h3>
          <p>Evaluates workload health, schema integrity, and exact transaction consistency without holes.</p>
          <code>Contiguous levels</code>
        </div>
        <div class="pipeline-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</div>
        <div class="pipeline-card">
          <span class="step-num">05</span>
          <h3>Attest & gate</h3>
          <p>Detached Ed25519 signature locks evidence bytes; CI gate blocks deployment on failed drills.</p>
          <code>Attested report</code>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="quickstart-band" id="quickstart">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-index">03 / QUICK START</p>
          <h2>Verify your first restore drill.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="under-link" href="/docs/start/">Complete installation guide <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="quickstart-grid">
        <div class="quickstart-step">
          <div class="step-badge">1</div>
          <h3>Install CLI & validate a drill</h3>
          <p>Install Checkride into a virtualenv and validate a drill contract without connecting to any cluster.</p>
          <pre><code>pip install checkride
checkride validate examples/drills/shop-namespace-loss.yaml</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="quickstart-step">
          <div class="step-badge">2</div>
          <h3>Run the isolated PostgreSQL drill</h3>
          <p>Creates two disposable k3d clusters, injects source loss, restores into target, and captures evidence.</p>
          <pre><code>make lab-up
python3 scripts/lab/restore.py --output /tmp/drill.json
make lab-down</code></pre>
        </div>
        <div class="quickstart-step">
          <div class="step-badge">3</div>
          <h3>Evaluate report & verify signature</h3>
          <p>Turn evidence into a V0–V4 report with phase RTO, then verify its detached Ed25519 attestation.</p>
          <pre><code>go run ./cmd/checkride-report /tmp/drill.json
go run ./cmd/checkride-attest sign \
  --evidence /tmp/drill.json \
  --key signing-key.pem \
  --output /tmp/drill.attestation.json</code></pre>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="comparison-band">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-index">04 / HOW CHECKRIDE COMPARES</p>
          <h2>Beyond green backup checkboxes.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="under-link" href="/comparison/">Full comparison details <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-table-wrapper">
        <table class="home-comparison-table">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th>Capability</th>
              <th>Standard backup tools</th>
              <th>Kymaros</th>
              <th>Databasus</th>
              <th class="checkride-col">Checkride</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Restore environment</strong></td>
              <td>In-place overwrite or manual</td>
              <td>Sandbox namespace (shared cluster)</td>
              <td>Docker container</td>
              <td class="checkride-col"><strong>Isolated separate cluster (default)</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Verification depth</strong></td>
              <td>V0 (Backup completed)</td>
              <td>V1–V2 (Velero status & pod health)</td>
              <td>V3 (Table row counts)</td>
              <td class="checkride-col"><strong>V0–V4 (Data correctness & invariants)</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>RTO measurement</strong></td>
              <td>Not measured</td>
              <td>Total test duration</td>
              <td>Container startup time</td>
              <td class="checkride-col"><strong>Phase-by-phase breakdown & SLA gate</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>RPO calculation</strong></td>
              <td>Snapshot timestamp</td>
              <td>Unmeasured</td>
              <td>Unmeasured</td>
              <td class="checkride-col"><strong>Exact acknowledged-write ledger</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Evidence integrity</strong></td>
              <td>Job log output</td>
              <td>CRD status in Kubernetes</td>
              <td>Terminal logs</td>
              <td class="checkride-col"><strong>Detached Ed25519 signature sidecars</strong></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td><strong>Evaluation engine</strong></td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td>Kubernetes Operator</td>
              <td>Local script</td>
              <td class="checkride-col"><strong>Go engine (CLI, API, CI gate, in-browser WASM)</strong></td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="workbench-band">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-index">05 / THE WORKBENCH</p>
          <h2>One drill. Inspectable end to end.</h2>
        </div>
        <a class="under-link" href="/product/">How the system fits together <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
      <figure class="studio-shot">
        <img src="/images/studio-preview.png" alt="Checkride Studio design view with a fictional namespace-loss drill specification, its live plan and V0–V4 verification depth" width="1440" height="900" loading="lazy" />
        <figcaption>
          <span>CHECKRIDE STUDIO / DESIGN DRILL & REPORT REVIEW</span>
          <span>Full Go verifier runs inside your browser via WebAssembly. No cluster connection required.</span>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="workbench-actions">
        <a class="action-primary" href="/demo/index.html#/report">Launch Studio in your browser <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="paths-band">
    <div class="page-wrap">
      <div class="paths-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="section-index">06 / CHOOSE A WORKFLOW</p>
          <h2>Start with the proof you need.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Three ways in. Each answers a different recovery question.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="paths-grid">
        <article>
          <p class="path-index">01 / IN YOUR BROWSER</p>
          <h3>Inspect a report</h3>
          <p>Explore the full Studio with sample evidence and the recorded lab run. The demo evaluates evidence; it does not connect to Kubernetes.</p>
          <a class="under-link" href="/demo/index.html#/report">Open the browser demo <span>↗</span></a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="path-index">02 / LOCAL VALIDATION</p>
          <h3>Check a drill spec</h3>
          <p>Install the CLI, validate a drill contract and catch invalid fields before planning a recovery exercise. Validation does not execute a restore.</p>
          <a class="under-link" href="/docs/start/">Follow the CLI setup <span>↗</span></a>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="path-index">03 / DISPOSABLE K3D LAB</p>
          <h3>Run one isolated restore</h3>
          <p>Requires Docker, k3d, kubectl, Python and Go. This V0–V3 drill deletes its source namespace after backup; use only the dedicated disposable clusters.</p>
          <a class="under-link" href="/docs/guides/k3d-isolated-restore/">Read the lab walkthrough <span>↗</span></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="next-band">
    <div class="page-wrap next-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="section-index">07 / WHAT IS NOT HERE YET</p>
        <h2>Evidence first.<br /><span>Automation next.</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="next-copy">
        <p>Checkride is pre-alpha: one PostgreSQL lab path is executable. General-purpose orchestration, automated scheduling, and complete V4 business checks are in active development.</p>
        <a class="action-primary" href="/roadmap/">See the implementation roadmap <span>↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ProductLayout>

<style>
  .hero-badges { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .badge { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 4px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; font: 500 10px var(--mono); color: var(--muted); background: var(--surface); letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .badge-accent { color: var(--mint); border-color: rgba(93, 240, 173, 0.3); }
  .badge-link { color: var(--text); transition: border-color .15s, color .15s; }
  .badge-link:hover { border-color: var(--mint); color: var(--mint); }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; }

  .pipeline-band { padding: 80px 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); }
  .heading-sub { color: var(--muted); font-size: 13px; margin: 6px 0 0; }
  .pipeline-steps { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-top: 36px; }
  .pipeline-card { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 22px 18px; border: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); border-radius: 6px; min-height: 190px; }
  .step-num { font: 500 12px var(--mono); color: var(--mint); margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .pipeline-card h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .pipeline-card p { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); flex: 1; }
  .pipeline-card code { display: inline-block; padding: 3px 6px; font: 9.5px var(--mono); color: var(--mint); background: rgba(93, 240, 173, 0.08); border-radius: 3px; align-self: flex-start; }
  .pipeline-arrow { color: var(--quiet); font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; }

  .quickstart-band { padding: 80px 0; background: var(--bg); }
  .quickstart-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 24px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .quickstart-step { padding: 24px 20px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 6px; background: var(--surface); }
  .step-badge { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 28px; height: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--mint); border-radius: 50%; color: var(--mint); font: 500 12px var(--mono); margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .quickstart-step h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; }
  .quickstart-step p { margin: 0 0 14px; font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted); min-height: 40px; }
  .quickstart-step pre { margin: 0; padding: 12px 14px; background: var(--bg); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 4px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .quickstart-step code { font: 10.5px var(--mono); color: var(--mint); line-height: 1.6; }

  .comparison-band { padding: 80px 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface); }
  .comparison-table-wrapper { overflow-x: auto; margin-top: 32px; }
  .home-comparison-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; text-align: left; font-size: 12px; }
  .home-comparison-table th { padding: 14px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; }
  .home-comparison-table td { padding: 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--muted); vertical-align: top; }
  .home-comparison-table tr:hover td { background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02); }
  .home-comparison-table .checkride-col { background: rgba(93, 240, 173, 0.05); color: var(--text); border-inline: 1px solid rgba(93, 240, 173, 0.2); }
  .home-comparison-table th.checkride-col { color: var(--mint); border-top: 2px solid var(--mint); }

  .workbench-actions { display: flex; justify-content: center; margin-top: 24px; }

  .paths-band { padding: 76px 0 82px; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); }
  .paths-heading { display: flex; align-items: end; justify-content: space-between; gap: 28px; margin-bottom: 30px; }
  .paths-heading h2 { margin: 12px 0 0; font-size: 32px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.15; }
  .paths-heading > p { max-width: 300px; margin: 0 0 3px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .paths-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 34px; }
  .paths-grid article { display: flex; min-width: 0; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; padding-top: 16px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .path-index { margin: 0 0 17px; color: var(--quiet); font: 9px var(--mono); }
  .paths-grid h3 { margin: 0 0 9px; font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; }
  .paths-grid article > p:not(.path-index) { flex: 1; margin: 0 0 18px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.8; }
  .signal-proof { color: var(--quiet); font-size: 9.5px; }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .pipeline-steps { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 16px; }
    .pipeline-arrow { display: none; }
    .quickstart-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .paths-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .paths-band, .quickstart-band, .pipeline-band, .comparison-band { padding-block: 54px; }
    .paths-heading { align-items: flex-start; flex-direction: column; gap: 11px; margin-bottom: 25px; }
    .paths-heading h2 { font-size: 27px; }
    .home-comparison-table th, .home-comparison-table td { padding: 10px 12px; font-size: 11px; }
  }
</style>